WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.053 --> 00:00:02.383
(ominous, heavy music)
- [Voiceover] Are you ready?

00:00:02.383 --> 00:00:04.302
Okay, good afternoon ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:04.302 --> 00:00:05.903
Welcome to Brooklyn, Wisconsin.

00:00:05.903 --> 00:00:07.915
We're about to start the
competition here today,

00:00:07.915 --> 00:00:09.776
and anytime you guys are ready to pull,

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.346
well you go ahead and
pull and never mind me.

00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:13.179
- Steady!

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.492
(ominous music)

00:00:15.492 --> 00:00:17.372
(grunting)

00:00:17.372 --> 00:00:19.641
- [Voiceover] Tighter!

00:00:19.641 --> 00:00:23.014
- [Voiceover] Tug-O-War is
the ultimate team sport.

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:25.263
If one man goes down,

00:00:25.263 --> 00:00:27.571
he can take the whole team down with him.

00:00:27.571 --> 00:00:29.001
'Cause you have to have
eight pullers workin'

00:00:29.001 --> 00:00:30.501
in unison, as one.

00:00:31.803 --> 00:00:32.810
- [Voiceover] Keep that,
keep that, keep that!

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.763
- [Voiceover] Push! Push!
(grunting)

00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:36.133
- To the general public,

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.545
they think Tug-O-War may be just a game

00:00:38.545 --> 00:00:39.721
in high school.

00:00:39.721 --> 00:00:41.160
- Low, keep it low!

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.689
- In serious competition,
there are strict rules

00:00:43.689 --> 00:00:46.885
and guidelines, and only the top athletes

00:00:46.885 --> 00:00:48.969
in the countries get to that level.

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:50.455
- Center, keep it on the center.

00:00:50.455 --> 00:00:51.446
- [Voiceover] Keep her down, boys.

00:00:51.446 --> 00:00:52.279
Keep her down!

00:00:52.279 --> 00:00:53.901
- [Herb] If you're goin' into a rope pull,

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.233
you might be the strongest
person in the world,

00:00:56.233 --> 00:00:57.632
but if your head isn't in it,

00:00:57.632 --> 00:00:58.637
you're gonna lose.

00:00:58.637 --> 00:00:59.920
(grunting)

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.729
- [Voiceover] Push! Push!

00:01:01.729 --> 00:01:03.144
- [Voiceover] (mumbling)
Cut it back! Cut it back!

00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:04.529
Keep it there! Keep 'em back!

00:01:04.529 --> 00:01:05.884
- [Voiceover] Back to positions, guys!

00:01:05.884 --> 00:01:08.726
There you go. There you go! (mumbling)

00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:09.559
(sighing)

00:01:09.559 --> 00:01:10.705
- [Voiceover] Good job, guys.

00:01:10.705 --> 00:01:12.507
(fast piano music)

00:01:12.507 --> 00:01:15.137
- [Herb] Your legs are the
strongest muscles in your body

00:01:15.137 --> 00:01:18.237
and they can push 400 pounds, easy.

00:01:18.237 --> 00:01:20.851
And you gotta transfer
that through your hands.

00:01:20.851 --> 00:01:22.223
They're not allowed to wear gloves.

00:01:22.223 --> 00:01:23.817
They can only put the tack on.

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.166
Calluses build up.

00:01:25.166 --> 00:01:29.544
I call 'em square fingers,
'cause you get the edges pushed.

00:01:29.544 --> 00:01:33.308
I got involved with
Tug-O-War when I was drunk.

00:01:33.308 --> 00:01:35.780
I was at a softball tournament,

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.887
and a friend of mine from high
school said they were short

00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:40.337
and needed an extra puller.

00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:41.755
And I said, "Okay."

00:01:41.755 --> 00:01:44.695
I've been pulling ever since.

00:01:44.695 --> 00:01:46.487
(somber, heavy music)
- Try it again.

00:01:46.487 --> 00:01:47.320
Set!

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:49.430
- Well, the reason that
Tug-O-War was ousted

00:01:49.430 --> 00:01:53.045
from the Olympics is that
they were cutting sports,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:54.176
so they dropped it.

00:01:54.176 --> 00:01:55.474
And that's been the fight:

00:01:55.474 --> 00:01:56.849
to get it back in.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:57.682
- [Voiceover] Push!

00:01:57.682 --> 00:01:59.484
- [Herb] I hope to see
it back in the Olympics

00:01:59.484 --> 00:02:01.797
'cause I believe it deserves to be there.

00:02:01.797 --> 00:02:03.912
I'm representing the US,

00:02:03.912 --> 00:02:06.527
and I take a lotta pride in
trying to do the best job

00:02:06.527 --> 00:02:08.686
I possibly can.
- [Voiceover] Push! Push!

00:02:08.686 --> 00:02:11.936
Push!
(heavy breathing)

